<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<CustomPermission xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        WHY THIS EXISTS (2026-08-28). TransactionTaskService completes checklist Tasks with
        plain user-mode DML, which requires Task object Edit. PROVEN that no permission set can
        grant that: ObjectPermissions.SobjectType is a RESTRICTED PICKLIST of 3,007 values, and
        Task / Event / Activity are NOT among them (Account/Contact/Lead/Opportunity/Case/
        Contract all are) — a direct API insert of an ObjectPermissions row for Task returns
        INVALID_OR_NULL_FOR_RESTRICTED_PICKLIST on SobjectType. Task CRUD can only be granted by
        a PROFILE on this platform, and profile changes are explicitly ruled out here.

        The agreed alternative: gate the write in the application with this custom permission
        and let TransactionTaskService's DML run in system mode. Sharing still applies — record-
        level security is untouched; only object-level CRUD is bypassed, and only on the Task
        completion/update path this permission authorizes.

        🔴 THE API NAME IS PINNED — Transaction_Task_Actions — a parallel developer stream is
        coding TransactionTaskService against this exact name via
        FeatureManagement.checkPermission('Transaction_Task_Actions'). Do not rename.

        Granted through permissionsets/DPEG_Task_Edit.permissionset-meta.xml, which is already a
        member of the DPEG_Transaction_Team permission set group — membership-only, same pattern
        as Transaction_Stage_Actions.customPermission-meta.xml (see that file's header for the
        full layer-4/membership-only rationale; this is not a new authorization layer).

        SCOPE IS TRANSACTION ONLY. DispositionTaskService has the identical Task-CRUD defect but
        needs its own permission decision from the user — this file does not cover Disposition,
        and no Disposition equivalent should be created on the strength of this one.
    -->
    <label>Transaction Task Actions</label>
    <description>Authorization letting TransactionTaskService complete/update checklist Tasks in system mode. Exists because Task object CRUD cannot be granted via any permission set on this platform (SobjectType restricted picklist) and profile changes are ruled out.</description>
    <isLicensed>false</isLicensed>
</CustomPermission>
